_Algeria)\nThis is a [dynamic list](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Wikipedia:WikiProject_Lists#Dynamic_lists) and may never be able to satisfy particular standards for completeness. You can help by [editing the page](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Special:EditPage\/2026_in_Algeria) to add missing items, with references to [reliable sources](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Wikipedia:Reliable_sources).\nEvents in the year  2026 in Algeria .\n## Incumbents\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=1) ]\n[President](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/President_of_Algeria): [Abdelmadjid Tebboune](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Abdelmadjid_Tebboune)\n[Prime Minister](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Prime_Minister_of_Algeria): [Sifi Ghrieb](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Sifi_Ghrieb)\n## Events\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=2) ]\n### January\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=3) ]\n4 January – President Tebboune dismisses [Bank of Algeria](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Bank_of_Algeria) governor Salah Eddine Taleb by presidential [decree](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Decree), and appoints [deputy governor](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Deputy_governor) Mouatassem Boudiaf as [acting governor](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Acting_governor). [  [ 1 ]  ](#cite_note-1)\n### March\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=4) ]\n4 March – At least six people are killed and 15 others are injured when a passenger bus and a [semi-trailer truck](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Semi-trailer_truck) collide in [Tamacine](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Tamacine), [Touggourt Province](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Touggourt_Province). [  [ 2 ]  ](#cite_note-2)\n5 March – Two people are killed and four others are injured when a [Beechcraft 1900](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Beechcraft_1900) of the [Algerian Air Force](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Algerian_Air_Force) crashes at [Boufarik Airport](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Boufarik_Airport) near [Boufarik](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Boufarik), [Blida Province](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Blida_Province). [  [ 3 ]  ](#cite_note-3)\n13 March – Seven militants are killed by the [Algerian Army](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Algerian_Army) during two counter-terrorism operations in [Tebessa Province](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Tébessa_Province); three soldiers are also killed in the clashes. [  [ 4 ]  ](#cite_note-4)\n### April\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=5) ]\n13 April –\n[Pope Leo XIV](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Pope_Leo_XIV) arrives in [Algiers](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Algiers) for a two-day visit, becoming the first pontiff to visit Algeria. [  [ 5 ]  ](#cite_note-5)\nTwo bombers die in a [suicide attack](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/2026_Blida_attacks) near a police station in [Blida](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Blida). [  [ 6 ]  ](#cite_note-6)\n20 April – Former industry minister [Ali Aoun](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Ali_Aoun) is sentenced to five years' imprisonment for corruption by a court in [Algiers](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Algiers) over the irregular sale of ferrous and non-ferrous metal waste. [  [ 7 ]  ](#cite_note-7)\n23 April – A boat carrying migrants from Somalia capsizes off [Bou Ismaïl](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Bou_Ismaïl), killing 17 passengers. [  [ 8 ]  ](#cite_note-8)\n### May\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=6) ]\n1 May – China lifts tariffs on imports from Algeria until 2028. [  [ 9 ]  ](#cite_note-9)\n### June\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=7) ]\n11 June–19 July – Algeria participates at the [2026 FIFA World Cup](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/2026_FIFA_World_Cup).\n### July\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=8) ]\n2 July – [2026 Algerian parliamentary election](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/2026_Algerian_parliamentary_election): The [FLN](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/National_Liberation_Front_(Algeria)) wins a plurality of seats in the [People's National Assembly](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/People). [  [ 10 ]  ](#cite_note-10)\n11 July – Mali restores diplomatic relations with Algeria after a yearlong rift. [  [ 11 ]  ](#cite_note-11)\n16 July – A fire at an orphanage in the Mohammadia district of [Algiers](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Algiers) kills 11 people and injures 19 others. [  [ 12 ]  ](#cite_note-12)\n24 July – The United States imposes a 12.5% tariff on Algeria, citing the presence of alleged forced labour in the supply chain. [  [ 13 ]  ](#cite_note-13)\n31 July – A bus plunges into a ravine near [Boumerdès](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Boumerdès), killing 28 people. [  [ 14 ]  ](#cite_note-14)  President Tebboune declares three days of national mourning for the victims. [  [ 15 ]  ](#cite_note-15)\n### August\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=9) ]\n4 August – Seventeen migrants are reported dead after attempting to cross from Algeria to [Spain](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Spain)'s [Balearic Islands](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Balearic_Islands), with two survivors. [  [ 16 ]  ](#cite_note-16)\n26 August – Multiple heatwave-caused wildfires kill 12 people and injure 54, across several provinces. [  [ 17 ]  ](#cite_note-17)\n### September\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=10) ]\n6 September – A 10-year-old boy is found dead in a well in [Ghassoul](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Ghassoul), [El Bayadh Province](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/El_Bayadh_Province), bringing an end to a four-day rescue operation which drew national attention. [  [ 18 ]  ](#cite_note-18)\n10 September – Algeria severs diplomatic relations with the United Arab Emirates, citing unspecified \"provocative or hostile\" acts. [  [ 19 ]  ](#cite_note-19)\n### Scheduled\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?title=2026_in_Algeria&action=edit&section=11) ]\n[2025–26 in Algerian football](https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/2025–26_in_Algerian_football) [  [ 20 ]  ](#cite_note-20)\n## Holidays\n[ [ edit ](\/w\/index.php?tit\n\n... [Truncated 26109 additional characters]"
